WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
[Cheers and applause]

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.500
(Mouthing): Thank you!

3
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:19.000
Chief Justice Roberts, President Carter,
President Clinton, President Bush,

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.250
President Obama, fellow Americans,
and people of the world, thank you.

5
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.750
[Cheers and applause]

6
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:38.500
We, the citizens of America, are
now joined in a great national effort

7
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:45.500
to rebuild our country and restore
its promise for all of our people.

8
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.250
Together we will determine the
course of America, and the world,

9
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.500
for many, many years to come.

10
00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.250
We will face challenges,
we will confront hardships,

11
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.750
but we will get the job done.

12
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.850
Every four years, we
gather on these steps

13
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:12.100
to carry out the orderly and
peaceful transfer of power –

14
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:19.000
and we are grateful to President Obama,
and first lady Michelle Obama,

15
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.500
for their gracious aid
throughout this transition.

16
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.000
They have been magnificent.
Thank you.

17
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.000
[Cheers and applause]

18
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:39.250
Today's ceremony, however,
has very special meaning –

19
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:43.500
because today, we are not
merely transferring power

20
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.350
from one administration to another,
or from one party to another –

21
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:53.000
but we are transferring power
from Washington DC,

22
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.500
and giving it back to you, the people.

23
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.000
[Cheers and applause]

24
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.000
For too long, a small group
in our nation's capital

25
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.250
has reaped the rewards of government,
while the people have borne the cost.

26
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:23.250
Washington flourished, but the
people did not share in its wealth.

27
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.500
Politicians prospered, but the
jobs left, and the factories closed.

28
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:38.000
The establishment protected itself,
but not the citizens of our country.

29
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.700
Their victories have
not been your victories;

30
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.000
their triumphs have not
been your triumphs;

31
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
and while they celebrated
in our nation's capital,

32
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:57.500
there was little to celebrate for
struggling families all across our land.

33
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.000
[Cheers and applause]

34
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:09.250
That all changes, starting
right here and right now,

35
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.000
because this moment is your
moment: it belongs to you.

36
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.500
[Cheers and applause]

37
00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.000
It belongs to everyone
gathered here today,

38
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.650
and everyone watching
all across America;

39
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.500
this is your day, this
is your celebration,

40
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.500
and this, the United States
of America, is your country.

41
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.500
[Cheers and applause]

42
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:49.000
What truly matters is not which
party controls our government,

43
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.500
but whether our government
is controlled by the people.

44
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.600
[Distant cheers and applause]

45
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:04.500
January 20th, 2017, will
be remembered as the day

46
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.000
the people became the
rulers of this nation again.

47
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.000
[Cheers and applause]

48
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:20.750
The forgotten men and women of our 
country will be forgotten no longer.

49
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.750
[Cheers and applause]

50
00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.250
Everyone is listening to you now.

51
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:32.600
You came by the tens of millions
to become part of a historic movement,

52
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.000
the likes of which the world
has never seen before.

53
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.500
[Distant cheers and applause]

54
00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.750
At the centre of this movement

55
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:52.000
is a crucial conviction that a
nation exists to serve its citizens.

56
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.350
Americans want great
schools for their children,

57
00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:01.000
safe neighbourhoods for their families,
and good jobs for themselves.

58
00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:12.100
These are just and reasonable demands
of righteous people and a righteous public.

59
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.250
But for too many of our citizens,
a different reality exists:

60
00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:22.000
mothers and children trapped
in poverty in our inner cities;

61
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:29.150
rusted out factories scattered like tombstones
across the landscape of our nation;

62
00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.250
an education system flushed with cash,

63
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:39.000
but which leaves our young and beautiful
students deprived of all knowledge;

64
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.500
and the crime, and the gangs, and the
drugs that have stolen too many lives

65
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.750
and robbed our country of
so much unrealised potential.

66
00:05:52.750 --> 00:06:00.500
This American carnage stops
right here and stops right now.

67
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.000
[Cheers and applause]

68
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:13.500
We are one nation, and
their pain is our pain,

69
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:19.750
their dreams are our dreams, and
their success will be our success.

70
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:26.900
We share one heart, one home,
and one glorious destiny.

71
00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:34.250
The oath of office I take today is an
oath of allegiance to all Americans.

72
00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.500
[Distant cheers and applause]

73
00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.600
For many decades, we've
enriched foreign industry

74
00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:49.250
at the expense of American industry;
subsidised the armies of other countries,

75
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:54.750
while allowing for the very
sad depletion of our military;

76
00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:01.500
we've defended other nations' borders,
while refusing to defend our own;

77
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.500
[Cheers and applause]

78
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:12.750
and spent trillions and
trillions of dollars overseas,

79
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:18.750
while America's infrastructure has
fallen into disrepair and decay.

80
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:25.150
We've made other countries rich,
while the wealth, strength,

81
00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:31.250
and confidence of our country
has dissipated over the horizon.

82
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:38.000
One by one, the factories
shuttered and left our shores,

83
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.750
with not even a thought
about the millions and

84
00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:46.250
millions of American workers
that were left behind.

85
00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:52.250
The wealth of our middle class
has been ripped from their homes,

86
00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:57.100
and then redistributed
all across the world.

87
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:05.250
But that is the past – and now,
we are looking only to the future.

88
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.500
[Cheers and applause]

89
00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:19.100
We assembled here today
are issuing a new decree

90
00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:25.350
to be heard in every city, in every foreign
capital, and in every hall of power;

91
00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:32.000
from this day forward, a new
vision will govern our land –

92
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:42.000
from this day forward, it's going to
be only 'America first,' 'America first.'

93
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.500
[Cheers and applause]

94
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:55.250
Every decision on trade, on taxes,
on immigration, on foreign affairs,

95
00:08:55.250 --> 00:09:00.250
will be made to benefit American
workers and American families.

96
00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.500
We must protect our borders from
the ravagers of other countries,

97
00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:11.750
making our products, stealing our
companies, and destroying our jobs.

98
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.500
[Cheers and applause]

99
00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.500
Protection will lead to great
prosperity and strength.

100
00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:28.000
I will fight for you with
every breath in my body,

101
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.000
and I will never ever let you down.

102
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.500
[Resonant cheers and applause]

103
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:42.500
America will start winning again,
winning like never before.

104
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.000
[Cheers and applause]

105
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:52.000
We will bring back our jobs,
we will bring back our borders,

106
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:58.400
we will bring back our wealth,
and we will bring back our dreams.

107
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.500
[Cheers and applause]

108
00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:09.750
We will build new roads, and
highways, and bridges, and airports,

109
00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:15.250
and tunnels, and railways,
all across our wonderful nation.

110
00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:21.250
We will get our people off
of welfare, and back to work,

111
00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:26.500
rebuilding our country with
American hands and American labour.

112
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.500
[Cheers and applause]

113
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:37.750
We will follow two simple rules:
'Buy American' and 'Hire American.'

114
00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.000
[Cheers and applause]

115
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.650
We will seek friendship and goodwill
with the nations of the world,

116
00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.500
but we do so with the understanding

117
00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:55.000
that it is the right of all nations
to put their own interests first.

118
00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:59.800
We do not seek to impose
our way of life on anyone –

119
00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.500
but rather, to let it
shine as an example;

120
00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.850
we will shine for
everyone to follow.

121
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.500
[Cheers and applause]

122
00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.500
We will reinforce old alliances
and form new ones,

123
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:21.350
and unite the civilised world
against radical Islamic terrorism,

124
00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:26.000
which we will eradicate completely
from the face of the earth!

125
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.500
[Cheers and applause]

126
00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:34.500
At the bedrock of our politics

127
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:38.500
will be a total allegiance to
the United States of America,

128
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:41.250
and through our loyalty
to our country,

129
00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:46.000
we will rediscover our
loyalty to each other.

130
00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:50.000
When you open your
heart to patriotism,

131
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.500
there is no room for prejudice.

132
00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.500
[Cheers and applause]

133
00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:06.000
The Bible tells us how
good and pleasant it is

134
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.750
when God's people live
together in unity.

135
00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:15.750
We must speak our minds openly,
debate our disagreements honestly,

136
00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:19.100
but always pursue solidarity.

137
00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:26.000
When America is united,
America is totally unstoppable.

138
00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:29.000
[Cheers and applause]

139
00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.250
There should be no fear –

140
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:38.750
we are protected, and we
will always be protected;

141
00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:41.500
we will be protected by the
great men and women

142
00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:45.000
of our military and
law enforcement,

143
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.000
and most importantly,

144
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.350
[Cheers and applause]

145
00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.250
we will be protected by God.

146
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.500
[Cheers and applause]

147
00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:03.850
Finally, we must think big,
and dream even bigger.

148
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:08.750
In America, we understand
that a nation is only living

149
00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.500
as long as it is striving.

150
00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:17.650
We will no longer accept politicians
who are all talk and no action –

151
00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:22.000
constantly complaining, but
never doing anything about it.

152
00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.000
[Cheers and applause]

153
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:37.500
The time for empty talk is over.
Now arrives the hour of action.

154
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.000
[Distant cheers and applause]

155
00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:48.150
Do not allow anyone to tell
you that it can not be done.

156
00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:53.750
No challenge can match the heart,
and fight, and spirit of America.

157
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:59.250
We will not fail; our country
will thrive and prosper again.

158
00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:04.750
We stand at the birth
of a new millennium –

159
00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:08.250
ready to unlock the
mysteries of space,

160
00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:11.750
to free the Earth from
the miseries of disease,

161
00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:17.600
and to harness the energies, industries,
and technologies of tomorrow.

162
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:25.250
A new national pride will stir our souls,
lift our sights, and heal our divisions.

163
00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:31.100
It's time to remember that old wisdom
our soldiers will never forget:

164
00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:36.000
that whether we are black,
or brown, or white,

165
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.500
we all bleed the same
red blood of patriots.

166
00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.750
[Cheers and applause]

167
00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:50.400
We all enjoy the same
glorious freedoms,

168
00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:54.900
and we all salute the
same great American flag.

169
00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.250
[Cheers and applause]

170
00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:04.400
And whether a child is born
in the urban sprawl of Detroit,

171
00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:07.250
or the windswept plains of Nebraska,

172
00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:13.250
they look up at the same night sky,
they fill their heart with the same dreams,

173
00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:20.750
and they are infused with the breath
of life by the same almighty creator.

174
00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.250
[Cheers and applause]

175
00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:32.150
So to all Americans, in every city
near and far, small and large –

176
00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:37.900
from mountain to mountain, from
ocean to ocean, hear these words:

177
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:41.500
you will never be ignored again.

178
00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.500
[Cheers and applause]

179
00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:54.000
Your voice, your hopes, and your
dreams will define our American destiny.

180
00:15:54.750 --> 00:16:00.000
And your courage and goodness and
love will forever guide us along the way.

181
00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:08.500
Together, we will make America strong
again, we will make America wealthy again,

182
00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:14.750
we will make America proud again,
we will make America safe again,

183
00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:20.750
and yes – together, we will
make America great again.

184
00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:25.100
Thank you, God bless you,
and God bless America.

185
00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:30.500
Thank you. God bless America.
